d=\"1173687740\">\n        <name>\n          <![CDATA[THE LAST VIKING]]>\n        </name>\n        <description>\n          <![CDATA[<div>\n<font size=\"5\"><b>The Last Viking&nbsp;</b></font><img src=\"https://d1bry8u3byci8.cloudfront.net/as-assets/variants/3vwbl3p3ll0419s4gnxo5ftb06u2/a6206d8b8848d1f5f779dd436f25589e3a792fee204effd13dccee565e881abd\" style=\"font-size:0.875rem;\">\n</div><div><font size=\"3\">Genre(s): Comedy/Crime/Drama</font></div><div><font size=\"3\">Denmark/Sweden | 2025 | 116 mins (Danish with <b>English Subtitles</b>)</font></div><div><font size=\"3\">Director:&nbsp;Anders Thomas Jensen</font></div><div><font size=\"3\">Stars:&nbsp;Mads Mikkelsen, Sofie Gr&aring;b&oslash;l, Nikolaj Lie Kaas, Lars Ranthe, John Lennon</font></div><div><p><font size=\"3\">Bank robber Anker entrusts the loot from\nhis latest robbery with his brother Manfred just before he is captured. On his\nrelease from prison, he seeks out his brother, but Manfred now believes himself\nto be John Lennon &ndash; and he cannot remember where the money is buried. Empathy\nbetween the brothers is not helped by Ankers&rsquo;s short temper. They return to\ntheir childhood holiday home, where the loot may be hidden, to work things out,\njoined by a group of other characters (played by Sofie Gr&aring;b&oslash;l and other\nwell-known faces from TV Scandi noir). A well-acted black comedy, full of\nhilarious misadventures and fun slapstick sequences.&nbsp;</font></p></div>]]>\n        </description>\n        <event_category></event_category>\n        <production_company_name></production_company_name>\n        <priority>0</priority>\n        <url>https://davidleancinema.ticketsolve.com/shows/1173687740/events</url>\n        <version>22</version>\n        <tags>\n        </tags>\n        <images>\n          <image priority=\"90\">\n            <url size=\"large\">https://d1bry8u3byci8.cloudfront.net/as-assets/variants/g85pq5p356t56poafmmd6ibzqdcf/a6206d8b8848d1f5f779dd436f25589e3a792fee